From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] search layered system configuration before vendor defaults
Source: https://github.com/ErikReider/SwayNotificationCenter/archive/refs/tags/v0.10.1.tar.gz
Upstream: Not submitted; this is a generic UAPI configuration proposal.

Install package defaults below /usr/share and search the normal user and
administrator XDG paths first. Add /run/xdg for temporary machine overrides,
then use the package files as the final fallback. Re-run that search on reload
instead of treating the file selected at startup as an explicit override.

Add a focused test for the full priority order. This keeps the behavior useful
on any normal Linux system and makes an empty higher-priority file mask lower
defaults.
